ta","data":[{"unit":1,"title":3,"area":125,"prev":127,"next":129,"titles":132,"firmware":301},{"id":2,"title":3,"aliases":4,"area":10,"order":11,"path":12,"context":13,"summary":18,"status":19,"firmware":20,"facts":25,"procedures":67,"parameters":83,"related":84,"body":87,"sources":88,"official_url":29,"controls":97},"sampler.slicing","Slicing a sample across the keys",[5,6,7,8,9],"slice mode","sample slicer","chop","transient slicing","tap slicing","sampler",40,"knowledge/manual/units/sampler/slicing.md",{"modes":14,"screens":16},[15],"instrument",[17],"M1","On a drum sampler track, `key + M1` cuts that key's sample into slices spread over the keyboard — at its transients, into equal parts, or where you tap.","current",{"min":21,"changed_in":22,"guide_version":23,"verified_on":24},"1.1.0",[],"1.1.15",null,[26,31,35,38,41,46,49,52,55,58,62],{"id":27,"text":28,"source":29,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":24,"confidence":30},"since","Slice mode arrived in OS 1.1.0.","https://teenage.engineering/downloads/op-xy#1.1.0","official",{"id":32,"text":33,"source":34,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":24,"confidence":30},"open","On a drum sampler track, `key + M1` opens the slicer for that key's sample.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/sample#sample-slicer",{"id":36,"text":37,"source":34,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":24,"confidence":30},"modes","`turn E1` chooses the mode: transient, even or tap.",{"id":39,"text":40,"source":34,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":24,"confidence":30},"layout","The slices fill the keyboard on their own and choke each other, so one slice sounds at a time.",{"id":42,"text":43,"source":44,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":24,"confidence":45},"max","With one slice per key, a sample gives at most 24 slices.","docs/research/30-presets-samples.md#32-counts-and-structure-limits","derived",{"id":47,"text":48,"source":34,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":24,"confidence":30},"transient","Transient mode cuts at the loudest hits; `turn E4` sets how many slices, and after pressing a slice's key `turn E2` and `turn E3` move its start and end.",{"id":50,"text":51,"source":34,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":24,"confidence":30},"even","Even mode splits a section into equal parts; `turn E2` and `turn E3` set where the section starts and ends, `turn E4` the count.",{"id":53,"text":54,"source":34,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":24,"confidence":30},"tap","In tap mode, tap `M1` to start the sample and again wherever a slice should begin; `M2` stops and lets the last slice run to the end.",{"id":56,"text":57,"source":34,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":24,"confidence":30},"tap-edit","In tap mode, press a slice's key and `turn E2` to move its start (the previous slice's end); `shift + key` deletes that slice.",{"id":59,"text":60,"source":61,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":24,"confidence":45},"confirm","The slicer screen offers cancel and done; which keys they sit on is not documented.","docs/research/50-hardware-ui.md#33-page-catalogue",{"id":63,"text":64,"source":65,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":24,"confidence":66},"tap-display","In tap mode the page shows a stop square on M2 and no slice count (one video, OS 1.x).","docs/research/78-overnight-accuracy.md#log","community",[68],{"id":69,"goal":70,"preconditions":71,"steps":74,"result":24,"source":34,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":24,"confidence":30},"slice-loop","Slice a drum loop at its hits",[72,73],"the loop is on a key of a drum sampler track","`M1` page",[75,78,80],{"keys":76,"note":77,"set":24},"key + M1","hold the key with the loop",{"keys":79,"note":47,"set":24},"turn E1",{"keys":81,"note":82,"set":24},"turn E4","number of slices",[],[85,86],"sampler.drum-sampler","sampler.drum-key-settings","Slicing turns one recording into a playable kit. Transient suits drums with clear hits, even suits\nloops cut to the grid, and tap marks musical phrases by ear while the sample plays.",[89,91,93,95,96],{"url":29,"kind":90},"changelog",{"url":34,"kind":92},"guide",{"url":44,"kind":94